            "review_title": "Review at Bun Dau Ngo Nho Phu Nho",
            "review_text": "yeonghaur\nSingapore, Singapore495 contributions\n0\nGood simple food, friendly service\nMar 2019 • Family\nChanced upon this simple local restaurant. At side alley, opposite secret garden. Nice wall painting. \n\nThey serve bun dau, an assortment of fried tofu, rice cakes, pork slices, bamboo shoots etc. Simple but delicious. One plate good for 2 costs 70k Dong. You can order extra. Similar to what I had eaten at northern Vietnam Ninh Binh, They also have noodle, fried pork which I didn’t try. \n\nFrequently mostly by locals. We were the only foreigners. No problem ordering though as menu has picture, and staff is very friendly. \n\nStrongly recommend for those who like simple meals.\nRead more\nWritten March 22, 2019",
